{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act criminal record screening limits","requirement":"A housing provider may not ask about or consider an applicant's criminal record before making a conditional offer, and after an offer may consider only certain recent or serious convictions, using an individualized assessment.","key_value":"No criminal record inquiry before a conditional offer","coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units; inquiry allowed on federal methamphetamine convictions and lifetime sex-offender registration.","penalty":"Monetary penalty up to $1,000 with no prior violation in five years, up to $5,000 with one prior, up to $10,000 with two or more priors in seven years; director may order cease and desist, remediation, or payment of up to $1,000 to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"P.L. 2021, c.110 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-55)","quoted_span":"A housing provider shall not require an applicant to complete any housing application that includes any inquiries regarding an applicant’s criminal record prior to the provision of a conditional offer","interaction":null,"confidence":0.95,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"application_screening_fees","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Fair Chance in Housing Act application fee disclosure","requirement":"Before accepting any application fee, a housing provider must disclose in writing whether its eligibility criteria include criminal history and that the applicant may submit evidence of inaccuracies, rehabilitation or mitigating factors. The director may order the fee returned.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Rental dwelling units offered for rent by a housing provider, other than a dwelling unit in an owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Excludes owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units"},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied premises of not more than four dwelling units.","penalty":"The director may require that the applicant's rental application fee be returned, unless housing is provided to the applicant.","effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"P.L. 2021, c.110 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-55)","quoted_span":"Prior to accepting any application fee, a housing provider shall disclose in writing to the applicant: (1) Whether the eligibility criteria of the housing provider include the review and consideration of criminal history; and (2) A statement that the applicant, pursuant to subsection a. of this section, may provide evidence demonstrating inaccuracies within the applicant's criminal record or evidence of rehabilitation or other mitigating factors.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D065-01","doc_id":"D065","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Eviction of former applicant after successful housing provider appeal","requirement":"If a housing provider's appeal succeeds and a court overturns the director's order, that determination is grounds to evict the former applicant who lives in the unit under that order, with at least 45 days' notice.","key_value":"45 days' notice","coverage_conditions":"Former applicants residing in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of a director's order under the Fair Chance in Housing Act.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":4,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"Applies to former applicants housed under a director's order"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2022-01-01","citation":"P.L. 2021, c.110 (N.J.S.A. 46:8-63)","quoted_span":"a determination that the housing provider did not violate the provisions of this act as evidenced by such successful appeal shall be grounds for the housing provider to evict the former applicant if that person resides in a rental dwelling unit owned by the housing provider as the result of the director’s order, so long as the housing provider provides the applicant with at least 45 days’ notice prior to the eviction","interaction":"Applies notwithstanding any provision of the Anti-Eviction Act, P.L.1974, c.49 (C.2A:18-61.1 et seq.).","confidence":0.85,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
